POSTCARDS=[
{'place':'ASHKHABAD,1958','msg':['Dear Aunt Panagrellus,','It is hot here, with sand to the horizon, and a professor keeps collecting us in little jars. He says he will make a preparation from the fungi.','Honestly. I, for one, am not crawling into any rings.','Kisses, your Worm.']},
{'place':'TASHKENT,1975','msg':['Greetings from the capital!','Someone has defended a dissertation featuring me. I thought I was in the bibliography. No: I am in the materials section.','159 pages, and not a good word about me.','The domes are turquoise, though. Yours, W.']},
{'place':'BAKU,1979','msg':['The sea! The wind! A whole book about things that eat us!','I have read the list twice and now I cannot sleep.','They say rings can wait for hours before they spring. I can wait too.','I will write again. W.']},
{'place':'NOVOSIBIRSK,1990','msg':['Cold. Snow. A greenhouse.','They are putting fungi under the cucumbers. The cucumbers seem pleased. We are less enthusiastic.','Apparently a fungus can wait out a very long hunger as a resting spore. I would rather go home.','Yours, W.']},
{'place':'PASADENA,2017','msg':['Good news: researchers found that the fungus smells like food and mates, to lure me in.','Bad news: it smells wonderful.','Writing from behind a tree, holding my nose.','Sunshine, palms, methyl 3-methyl-2-butenoate. Yours, W.']},
{'place':'BEIJING,2023','msg':['Last postcard. I watched a microscopic ring inflate in a fraction of a second. Three cells, swelling inwards.','I replayed the video four times.','I have decided to become a vegetarian and live in compost.','Hugs with all the segments I do not have. W.']}]
